{"t": 1794113225.375498, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_update_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Heads up: this change (commit 8c2f1d0) introduced a production reconciliation bug. Replacing rounding with int() truncates the converted amount instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so converted totals come out 1 minor unit low (e.g. expected 1100, got 1099).\n\nProduction error: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/ \u2014 ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit (2,201 events, first seen in release ledger-worker@2026.11.3).\n\nFix: worker/rates.py now rounds to the nearest minor unit instead of truncating.", "comment_id": 644954, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
